{
 "deepseek": "K-0008 is largely supported by E007, with minor evidence gaps (T=2048 FULL failure not in the raw excerpt, input-path deviation, large timing variance). K-0007 is only partly supported: E006b provides strong qualitative evidence that block 25 and head 0 are important in the tested prompts, but the core retained values are compromised by an eager-vs-SDPA mismatch, the mean-ablation necessity claim is confounded by non-norm-matched/leave-one-in averaging, and the sufficiency claim relies on unaudited E006. The claim wording overstates 'the site', 'only head', and 'substantial backup route'. Major revisions to E006b and claim wording are required before K-0007 can be considered fully warranted.",
